  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the file size limit on the GST portal?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Each uploaded document is capped at 5MB, and the number of attachments is limited by the filing type. This tool compresses every file under that cap automatically and warns you if a document cannot be brought under it without unacceptable quality loss."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I compress a PDF for the GST portal without making it unreadable?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Use a level that resamples images rather than degrading text. PDF text is vector data and is unaffected by compression at any level — only scanned pages and photographs get resampled. The Balanced preset targets around 150 DPI, which is comfortably legible for an officer reading on screen while typically cutting 40 to 55 percent of the size."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many documents can I attach to an SCN reply or an appeal?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The limits differ by filing type and the tool applies the correct one for the mode you choose, merging your documents into that number of attachments so you are not left trying to work it out at the deadline."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Why do annexures need labelling?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Because your reply refers to them. If your submission says \"as per Annexure 3\" and the officer cannot tell which uploaded file that is, the point does not land. Stamping sequential annexure labels and page numbers onto the pages makes the bundle navigable and is standard practice in any adjudication or appellate filing."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Is my notice and evidence uploaded to a server?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "No. Everything runs inside your browser. This matters more here than almost anywhere else on the site — a GST notice bundle contains your GSTIN, your turnover, your ledgers and often the department's allegations against you. None of it is transmitted, and there is no account holding a copy."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can I use this for APL-01 and APL-03 appeals?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. The Appeal mode is built for APL-01 and APL-03 filings and applies the corresponding attachment limit, alongside the same labelling, merging and compression steps."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What if a document still will not fit under 5MB?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "That normally means it is a high-resolution scan. Rescan at 200 to 300 DPI in greyscale rather than colour, which typically cuts the size dramatically, or split it into parts if the filing type allows more attachments. Dropping compression quality further tends to make small print unreadable, which is a worse outcome than an extra file."
        }
      },
